<section class="panel mb-4"><div class="panel-heading"><h2>Business reconciliation</h2><span class="mini-pill">{{ $from }} → {{ $to }}</span></div><div class="row g-4"><div class="col-md-6"><dl class="totals-list"><div><dt>Product sales after discounts</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['merchandise']) }}</dd></div><div><dt>Billed delivery</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['delivery']) }}</dd></div><div class="total"><dt>Sales revenue</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['revenue']) }}</dd></div><div><dt>Allocated stock costs</dt><dd>− {{ $money($summary['cost']) }}</dd></div><div><dt>Actual courier costs</dt><dd>− {{ $money($summary['courier']) }}</dd></div><div class="total"><dt>Gross profit</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['profit']) }}</dd></div></dl></div><div class="col-md-6"><dl class="totals-list"><div><dt>Cash collected, net refunds</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['cash']) }}</dd></div><div><dt>Payments pending · all active orders</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['pending']) }}</dd></div><div><dt>Refunds due · cancelled orders</dt><dd>{{ $money($summary['refunds']) }}</dd></div></dl><p class="small muted">Sales and profit use delivery dates in the selected period and currently delivered orders. Cash uses actual receipt/refund dates. Pending balances and refunds due are current, across all dates. Cancellations remove sales from delivery reports; cash and stock histories remain.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><h2>Batch investment & realised returns</h2></div><p class="small muted">All money is PKR. Merchandise revenue and order discounts follow dispatched batch quantities. Delivery and courier amounts appear only in the business totals above.</p><div class="table-responsive"><table class="table report-table"><thead><tr><th>Batch / pool</th><th>Purchase</th><th>Packaging</th><th>Branding</th><th>Other</th><th>Investment</th><th>Remaining in stock</th><th>Adjustment loss cost</th><th>Delivered quantity</th><th>Merchandise revenue</th><th>Realised stock cost</th><th>Merchandise profit</th></tr></thead><tbody>@forelse($batches as $b) @php($investment=$b->purchase+$b->packaging+$b->branding+$b->other) @php($loss=\App\Support\Money::allocate($investment,max(0,$b->original_quantity-$b->physical-($b->dispatched_quantity??0)),$b->original_quantity)) @php($remaining=max(0,$investment-($b->consumed_cost??0)-$loss))<tr><td><strong>{{ $b->reference }}</strong><small class="d-block muted">{{ $b->stock_key }} · {{ $b->received_on }}</small></td>@foreach(['purchase','packaging','branding','other'] as $c)<td>{{ $money($b->$c) }}</td>@endforeach<td>{{ $money($investment) }}</td><td>{{ $money($remaining) }}</td><td>{{ $money($loss) }}</td><td>{{ number_format($b->sold??0) }}</td><td>{{ $money($b->revenue) }}</td><td>{{ $money($b->realised_cost) }}</td><td>{{ $money(($b->revenue??0)-($b->realised_cost??0)) }}</td></tr>@empty<tr><td colspan="12" class="py-4 muted">Receive a batch to see its investment and returns here.</td></tr>@endforelse</tbody></table></div>{{ $batches->links() }}<p class="small muted mb-0">Batch investment = purchase + packaging + branding + other direct costs. Each component is counted once. Remaining investment covers physical stock, including reservations; dispatched quantities use their saved cost. Costs are allocated in paisa over original quantity, with rounding reconciled on final dispatch. Adjustment losses are shown separately and excluded from the defined gross profit. Merchandise profit = delivered merchandise revenue − saved stock cost.</p></section>
